---
layout: layout.njk
title: Budget Builder
seo_title: "Free Production Budget Builder with Excel Export | Tubes"
description: "Build a film or TV production budget in your browser: sections, lines, quantities, rates and percentages on top. Import a Movie Magic export, export to Excel, save up to ten versions."
permalink: /tools/budget-builder/
# Geen demo-popup en geen statistiek-script (zie "Gratis tools" in CLAUDE.md).
# Deze tool praat wél met de eigen server voor accounts en versies; server.js
# geeft /tools/budget-builder/ daarom een CSP met connect-src 'self'.
browser_only: true
sections:
  - type: hero
    kicker: Free tool
    title: Build a production *budget* and export it to Excel
    text: |
      Sections, lines, quantities and rates, with percentages such as contingency on top. Totals follow as you type. Start from the Movie Magic account structure, import an existing export, and download an Excel file in the layout Tubes uses.

      Everything stays in your browser: the budget and up to ten saved versions live on this device, and nothing is sent to us. Download a file to keep a copy or to open it on another computer.
---
{#- Gratis tool "Budget Builder". Bewust géén CMS-secties: het bewerkdeel is te
    specifiek. Tekst wijzig je hier, opmaak staat in style.css (blok "Gratis
    tools: Budget builder", klassen bb-*), logica in js/budget-builder.js. De
    lezer voor xlsx/CSV (import) is js/budget-compare.js, dat als bibliotheek
    meelaadt (window.BudgetCompare). Formaten staan in js/budget-templates.js. -#}

{#- data-storage: "local" = versies in de browser (actief); "account" = versies op de server met e-mail en wachtwoord (code blijft aanwezig). -#}
<section class="section theme-white bb-section" id="tool" data-budget-builder data-storage="local" data-max-lines="2000" data-max-versions="10">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="bb-top">
      <div class="bb-top-text">
        <h2>Build your budget</h2>
        <p>Add sections and lines, or pick a format under Templates. The budget is kept in this browser as you type. Save version keeps a named copy on this device, and a file download takes it anywhere.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bb-actions">
        <span class="bb-account" data-bb-account>Not signed in · <button type="button" class="bc-link-button" data-bb-login>Log in</button></span>
        <button type="button" class="button button-secondary bb-feedback-button" data-bb-open="feedback">Feedback</button>
        <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-open="import">Import</button>
        <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-open="templates">Templates</button>
        <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-open="export">Export</button>
        <button type="button" class="button button-primary" data-bb-save>Save version</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    {#- Stap 1: formaat kiezen. Tegels zolang het budget leeg is; daarna een
        smalle balk met het gekozen formaat en een knop om te wisselen. -#}
    <div class="bb-formats" data-bb-formats></div>

    <div class="bb-step-head"><span class="bb-step">2</span><h3>Budget details</h3><span class="bb-help">Name, production, currency, VAT and date. All optional, they appear on the Excel export.</span></div>
    <div class="bb-meta">
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-wide">Budget name <input type="text" data-bb-meta="name" placeholder="Draft 1" autocomplete="off"></label>
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-wide">Production <input type="text" data-bb-meta="production" placeholder="Working title" autocomplete="off"></label>
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-small">Currency <select data-bb-meta="currency">
        <option value="EUR">EUR</option>
        <option value="GBP">GBP</option>
        <option value="USD">USD</option>
        <option value="CHF">CHF</option>
        <option value="SEK">SEK</option>
        <option value="NOK">NOK</option>
        <option value="DKK">DKK</option>
        <option value="ISK">ISK</option>
        <option value="PLN">PLN</option>
        <option value="CZK">CZK</option>
        <option value="HUF">HUF</option>
        <option value="RON">RON</option>
        <option value="BGN">BGN</option>
        <option value="CAD">CAD</option>
        <option value="AUD">AUD</option>
      </select></label>
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-small">VAT % <input type="number" data-bb-meta="vat" min="0" max="100" step="0.5" inputmode="decimal"></label>
      <label class="bb-field bb-field-date">Date <input type="date" data-bb-meta="date"></label>
    </div>

    <p class="bb-notice" data-bb-notice role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>

    <div class="bb-layout">
      <div class="bb-main">
        <div class="bb-step-head"><span class="bb-step">3</span><h3>Sections and budget lines</h3><span class="bb-help">Pick cost types per section from the list, or add your own lines. Totals follow as you type.</span></div>
        <div class="bb-sections" data-bb-sections></div>
      </div>

      <aside class="bb-summary" data-bb-summary>
        <div class="bb-step-head"><span class="bb-step">4</span><h3>Totals, save and export</h3></div>
        <div class="bb-summary-card">
          <span class="bb-label">Total excl. VAT</span>
          <div class="bb-total" data-bb-total>0</div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row"><span>Lines subtotal</span><span class="bb-num" data-bb-subtotal>0</span></div>
          <div class="bb-additionals" data-bb-additionals></div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row bb-sum-add"><button type="button" class="bc-link-button" data-bb-add-additional>+ Add a percentage</button></div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row bb-sum-total"><span>Total excl. VAT</span><span class="bb-num" data-bb-total-excl>0</span></div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row"><span>VAT <span data-bb-vat-label>21%</span></span><span class="bb-num" data-bb-vat>0</span></div>
          <div class="bb-sum-row bb-sum-last"><span>Total incl. VAT</span><span class="bb-num" data-bb-total-incl>0</span></div>
          <div class="bb-summary-actions">
            <button type="button" class="button button-primary" data-bb-save>Save version</button>
            <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-open="export">Export</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bb-share" data-bb-share hidden>
          <span class="bb-label">Share per section</span>
          <div class="bb-share-list" data-bb-share-list></div>
        </div>
        <div class="bb-privacy" data-bb-how>
          <strong>How saving works</strong>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>As you type</strong>, the budget is stored in this browser. Close the tab and come back: it is still here.</li>
            <li><strong>Save version</strong> keeps a named copy on this device, up to ten. Open, rename or delete them under "versions" above.</li>
            <li><strong>This device only.</strong> Another computer, another browser or a cleared browser history does not have them.</li>
            <li><strong>Download as file</strong> for a copy you can keep, email or open elsewhere with "Open a file". Excel and CSV are under Export.</li>
            <li>Nothing is sent to us. Only the Feedback button sends what you type there.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#- Dialogen: account, versies, import, formaten, export -#}
  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="account">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3 data-bb-account-title>Save your budget</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">An account keeps up to ten versions of your budget and lets you open them on any device.</p>
    <div class="bb-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button type="button" class="bb-tab is-active" role="tab" data-bb-mode="register" aria-selected="true">Create an account</button>
      <button type="button" class="bb-tab" role="tab" data-bb-mode="login" aria-selected="false">I already have one</button>
    </div>
    <form class="bb-form" data-bb-account-form novalidate>
      <label>Work email <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required inputmode="email"></label>
      <label>Password <input type="password" name="password" autocomplete="current-password" required minlength="8"><span class="bb-help" data-bb-password-help>At least 8 characters</span></label>
      <label class="bb-consent" data-bb-consent-row><input type="checkbox" name="consent"> <span>Store my budget on the Tubes server (EU) and use my email address to reach me about this tool. No newsletter, no sharing with others. <a href="/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy notice</a></span></label>
      <p class="bb-form-error" data-bb-account-error role="alert"></p>
      <button type="submit" class="button button-primary" data-bb-account-submit>Create account and save</button>
    </form>
    <p class="bb-dialog-note">Until you save, the budget only lives in this browser. Saving sends it to your account; you can delete it there at any time.</p>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="versions">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Your versions</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro" data-bb-versions-intro>Up to ten versions of one budget, saved in this browser.</p>
    <div class="bb-versions" data-bb-versions></div>
    <div class="bb-dialog-actions">
      <button type="button" class="button button-primary" data-bb-save-new>Save current as a new version</button>
      <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-file-save>Download as file</button>
      <label class="button button-secondary bc-file">Open a file <input class="visually-hidden" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" data-bb-file-open></label>
      <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-logout>Log out</button>
    </div>
    <p class="bb-dialog-note" data-bb-versions-note>Versions stay on this device. A downloaded file (.json) is the way to keep a copy or to move a budget to another computer.</p>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="import">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Import a budget</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">A Movie Magic export (.xlsx), or any budget as Excel or CSV. Sections and lines are recognised the same way as in the <a href="/tools/budget-compare/">Free Production Budget Comparison Tool</a>; quantities become 1 and the amount becomes the rate.</p>
    <label class="button button-secondary bc-file">Choose a file <input class="visually-hidden" type="file" accept=".csv,.tsv,.txt,.xlsx" data-bb-import-file></label>
    <p class="bb-form-error" data-bb-import-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="bb-import-preview" data-bb-import-preview hidden>
      <p class="bb-help" data-bb-import-summary></p>
      <div class="bb-dialog-actions">
        <button type="button" class="button button-primary" data-bb-import-apply="replace">Replace the current budget</button>
        <button type="button" class="button button-secondary" data-bb-import-apply="append">Add as extra sections</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="templates">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Formats and templates</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">Choose the account structure you work with. More formats can be added; ask us if yours is missing.</p>
    <div class="bb-templates" data-bb-templates></div>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="feedback">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Feedback on the Budget Builder</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">Something missing, wrong or confusing? Tell us. It goes straight to the people who build this tool.</p>
    <form class="bb-form" data-bb-feedback-form novalidate>
      <label>Your feedback <textarea name="message" rows="5" required placeholder="What would make this tool more useful for you?"></textarea></label>
      <label>Email <span class="bb-help">(optional, if you would like a reply)</span> <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" inputmode="email"></label>
      <p class="bb-form-error" data-bb-feedback-error role="alert"></p>
      <button type="submit" class="button button-primary" data-bb-feedback-submit>Send feedback</button>
    </form>
    <p class="bb-dialog-note">Your message and email address are stored with our contact messages and used only to follow up on your feedback.</p>
  </dialog>

  <dialog class="bb-dialog" data-bb-dialog="export">
    <button type="button" class="bb-dialog-close" data-bb-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3>Export</h3>
    <p class="bb-dialog-intro">Files are generated in your browser; nothing is uploaded.</p>
    <div class="bb-export-list">
      <button type="button" class="bb-export-item" data-bb-export="xlsx"><strong>Excel (.xlsx)</strong><span>The layout Tubes exports: summary, lines with formulas, section rows, and a second sheet with totals per section.</span></button>
      <button type="button" class="bb-export-item" data-bb-export="csv"><strong>CSV</strong><span>One row per line, for any spreadsheet or the compare tool.</span></button>
      <button type="button" class="bb-export-item" data-bb-export="print"><strong>Print or save as PDF</strong><span>A clean print of sections, lines and totals.</span></button>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</section>

{%- set featureText %}
Every budget in Tubes is built the same way, section by section, and then keeps working after approval: purchase orders, invoices and actuals land on the same lines, so the cost report compares against the budget you actually approved.

This free builder covers the first step. When you want the rest, the Excel it exports opens in Tubes as is.
{% endset -%}
{%- set section = {
  theme: "teal",
  heading: "In Tubes the budget keeps going",
  lead: "From budget to cost control on the same lines",
  text: featureText,
  image: "/assets/images/tubes-budgeting.png",
  image_alt: "Budgeting in Tubes",
  button: { label: "See the Budgeting module", url: "/platform/" }
} -%}
{% include "partials/sections/feature.njk" %}

{%- set section = {
  theme: "white",
  heading: "Questions about this tool",
  items: [
    { question: "Where is my budget saved?",
      answer: "In your own browser, on this device. The budget you are working on is stored as you type, and Save version keeps up to ten named copies next to it. Nothing is sent to Tubes. Another computer or browser does not see these budgets, and clearing your browser data removes them." },
    { question: "How do I keep a copy or move it to another computer?",
      answer: "Under versions, choose Download as file: you get a small .json file with the whole budget. Keep it, email it, and load it anywhere with Open a file. For a spreadsheet, use Export for Excel or CSV." },
    { question: "Which formats can I import?",
      answer: "A Movie Magic Budgeting export (.xlsx, with its Topsheet, Categories and Account Details sheets), and any budget as Excel or CSV with a code, description and amount per line. Sections come from headings, a section column or the topsheet." },
    { question: "How does the Excel export look?",
      answer: "Like the export from Tubes: a title and summary, a table with Type, Description, Remarks, Qty, Unit, Price per unit and Budget Total, a row per section, formulas for the totals and a second sheet with totals per section." },
    { question: "Are prices or sales included?",
      answer: "No. This tool covers the cost side only. Quotations, sales prices and margins are part of Tubes itself." }
  ]
} -%}
{% include "partials/sections/faq.njk" %}

{%- set section = {
  title: "Ready to take the budget past the first step?",
  text: "Tubes carries the same lines through purchase orders, invoices and the cost report.",
  button: { label: "Request a Demo", url: "/contact/" }
} -%}
{% include "partials/sections/cta.njk" %}

<script src="{{ assets.budgetCompare }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ assets.budgetTemplates }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ assets.budgetBuilder }}" defer></script>
